a mountain lion is on its way back to  the wild after it decided to venture  into a summerlin neighborhood earlier  today  it made for quite the show for some in  the area orco mana spoke to a family who  was surprised by an  up-close encounter he joins us live now  with all the latest details orco  sasha after hours of roaming in the  neighborhoods here in the summerlin area  the  mountain lion was found here in front of  this home it was actually right here on  the front porch  police say luckily no one was injured  but it was still quite a shock to  everyone who saw it  videos and photos show the mountain lion  walking in between homes  police say they first got a call about a  mountain lion in the area of ulta  and fox hill drives around six this  morning but when officers  showed up the mountain lion got away it  was spotted again  around noon when it seemed to be hot and  tired police and  animal control were able to contain it  to a backyard and the nevada department  of wildlife tranquilized it  it still made its way to the front porch  after it was tranquilized but after it  stopped moving it was transported away  we spoke to a father and daughter who  were just going for a walk when they  came face to face with the wild animal  we looked to our left and this enormous  mountain lion was coming down the fence  line  stopped and looked at us and for the  first time  abby is my daughter abby and i felt real  fear  and that's when people were up on the  balconies  yelling at us to try to get out of there  we were really scared  once i realized when i started looking  left and right and realized that there  was fence on both sides of us  i got really worried and the lion was  going that way  and then we kept walking for about 10  minutes trying to find a way out  definitely not what you'd expect to see  when spending some father-daughter time  police tell us the mountain lion is  doing fine and will be released into the  wild  now if you ever spot a mountain lion or  another wild animal in your neighborhood  you're told to call 911 officers also  say the best thing to do if you can  is just go inside reporting live near  summerlin tonight orco mana 8 news now
 

